    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3eb5ed74-942b-5ed3-9330-8eca948c9f4c",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{6}{x0}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x0.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=1\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{x0}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot\\left(1\\,\\text{d}u\\right) \\\\ & =6\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\ & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x0|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
